-> it embeds a per-compilation cookie (`_sm100_cu_<hash>_<8 digits>`, a monotonic timestamp) into
-> `.shstrtab` / `.strtab`, so two compiles of *byte-identical, unmodified* source already differ
-> and a bare `cmp` always reports a difference. It proves nothing, and it can never report
-> "IDENTICAL".
->
-> **Use the recipe in `AI/sm120_touchpoints.md` → "No-regression check" instead.** It is a
-> four-step procedure: (1) sm100 `Normal` before-vs-after, (2) sm90 `MGroupedContiguous`
-> before-vs-after, both compared by `.text` sha256 or by a cookie-normalised whole-file hash;
-> (3) a **required** sensitivity probe that must report a *difference*, because an `IDENTICAL`
-> from steps 1-2 is meaningless until the comparison has been shown able to fail; and (4) the
-> `Batched` + `kSplitKFactor > 1` compile-error check. That file also records the results
-> obtained at the Task 5 commit.
->
-> Do not restore the `cmp` form, here or anywhere else.
