-- [ ] **Step 1: Enforce the CUDA floor**
-
-DeepJIT already asserts NVCC >= 12.9 (`backend.hpp`) but exposes no public version accessor,
-and sm120 needs 13.0. The right guard is compile-time, in the JIT-generated source: put it in
-a **Category A** device header that every sm120 kernel already includes, so it costs zero
-touchpoints and fires at the exact moment it matters — when the JIT invokes nvcc for an sm120
-kernel.
-
-At the top of `deep_gemm/include/deep_gemm/common/sm120_utils.cuh`, after the includes:
-
-```cuh
-// SM120 block-scaled MMA requires CUDA 13.0+. On 12.x, nvcc's
-// --gpu-architecture=sm_120a form was reported to drop block_scale
-// (see AI/2026-09-12-sm120-port-design.md section 3.1), which would
-// silently produce wrong numerics rather than fail to build.
-// DeepJIT's own floor is 12.9; this tightens it for sm120 only.
-#if defined(__CUDACC_VER_MAJOR__) && (__CUDACC_VER_MAJOR__ < 13)
-#error "DeepGEMM SM120 kernels require CUDA 13.0 or newer"
-#endif
-```
-
-Every sm120 device kernel includes this header (verified in Tasks 2-6), and the host
-extension does not, so this guards JIT compilation without affecting the sm90/sm100 build.
-
